# Check every text file out as LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows honours core.autocrlf and rewrites LF to CRLF at
# checkout time. That silently broke a fresh clone in two ways:
#
#   - lint.mjs tests for "---\n" to find SKILL.md's YAML frontmatter, so a CRLF
#     checkout reported "missing YAML frontmatter" and then "name undefined".
#   - index.json carries a SHA-256 per chapter, computed over LF content, so
#     every chapter looked like it had drifted from the index.
#
# Both tools are now tolerant of CRLF as well, but this is the root-cause fix:
# the corpus is LF, the hashes are over LF, and a checkout should match.
#
# CI on ubuntu-latest could never have caught it, because autocrlf is off there.
# The Windows job added alongside it exists for exactly this class of bug.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.zip   binary
